## What was missed, and why (7 MISSED rows; full scorecard: `docs/RESULTS.md`)

- % of oracle ceiling {{systems.lambdamart_ips.pct_of_ceiling_ndcg10|.1%}} (target 70%); localness index rho {{localness_validation.spearman_rho|.3f}} (target 0.6).
- Long-tail share {{longtail.share|.3f}} (target 0.25) and precision {{longtail.precision|.3f}}. **Two rows trace to targets set without reference to the data's
  baselines**: long-tail precision 0.40 (pool base rate {{derived.longtail_lift_over_base_rate.base_rate|.3f}}) and the within/cross-archetype ratio 2.0 (a perfect ranker reaches
  {{scenario4_diagnosis.post_fix.holdout_personalization_reference.perfect_ranker_within_cross_ratio|.2f}}); the recall 0.85 and chance-lift +0.35 targets were also set a priori and made the K rule infeasible (DR13).
- Decisions worth reading (DR3 objective, DR12 retrieval design, DR13 K selection): `docs/TECHNICAL.md` section 12.1. DR5 (ANN benchmark) not run; all data is synthetic.
